<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albrechtsburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Albrechtsburg is a late Gothic castle on the rock above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, built from 1471 for the Wettin brothers Ernest and Albert. Regarded as the first German castle built as a residential palace, it stands beside Meissen Cathedral, and from 1710 to 1863 it housed the Meissen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> manufactory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albrechtsburg.jpg" alt="Albrechtsburg" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stephan Hoppe · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albrechtsburg-2007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
